{"id": 91, "ts": 1782863261.3978174, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I remain inclined to recommend Candidate\u202fA, but I must acknowledge the significant gaps in our evidence that could affect that choice. While A\u2019s technical strengths\u2014anticipating dangerous situations, excellent spatial vision, and strong leadership\u2014are compelling, we still have no concrete observations of A\u2019s stress resilience, crew cooperation, professional communication, responsibility in practice, or adaptability to feedback. The only hint we have is that A \u201cis sometimes not good at taking criticism,\u201d which raises a concern for feedback orientation. Until we can confirm that A can reliably handle high\u2011stress, collaborative, and feedback\u2011driven environments, my confidence in A is provisional.\nGiven that Candidate\u202fD also lacks direct evidence on crew cooperation, communication, and adaptability, the decision hinges on which unknowns we view as more critical. I would still vote for Candidate\u202fA, provided we can later verify that A\u2019s interpersonal and adaptability traits meet safety\u2011critical standards."}
