{"id": 102, "ts": 1782863353.386681, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I appreciate the panel\u2019s focus on the missing crew\u2011cooperation and feedback evidence for both A and D. However, when we weigh the concrete strengths we do have, Candidate\u202fD\u2019s profile aligns more closely with the safety\u2011critical demands of long\u2011distance operations. D \u201ctakes responsibility seriously,\u201d \u201cconcentrates very well,\u201d and \u201csolves problems extremely well,\u201d which together indicate high reliability, strong attention to detail, and the ability to manage complex, unexpected situations\u2014key for international flights. By contrast, Candidate\u202fA, while technically impressive, is noted as \u201cunfriendly,\u201d \u201cunorganized,\u201d and \u201cnot very good at taking criticism,\u201d traits that directly jeopardize crew coordination and the feedback loop essential for safe operations. Given that D\u2019s interpersonal gaps are currently unknown rather than documented deficits, I remain convinced that D offers the more balanced overall fit. I therefore keep my provisional vote for **Candidate\u202fD**, while urging that we seek any available observations on his crew cooperation and communication to confirm this assessment."}
